# Run output at the repository root (kb/Work PB2608): a conformance golden's relative ASSIGN names its file in the
# working directory, so a by-hand `cobol run` from the root leaves .dat/.rpt/.txt files here, and a `git add -A` once
# committed thirteen of them (d8f9168e7). The suites run each program in its own directory; no root file is one of these.
/*.dat
/*.rpt
/*.txt

# ANTLR build outputs - regenerated by every build directly into Generated/ (java + pwsh prerequisites);
# never check in (DEVLOG 555/556)
src/Cobol.Net.Frontend/Generated/

# ANTLR IDE-plugin java-target caches — never source (build/IDE output; removed at rearch P1)
**/.antlr/

# gen-reserved-words.ps1 fetch cache (GnuCOBOL per-standard word lists — derived facts are committed, sources are not)
.cache/

.aider*
*.prt

# ── EXTERNAL DIFFERENTIAL CORPUS (plan §11 A4 / P14 Step 13) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚖ LICENSING (load-bearing — do NOT relax): GnuCOBOL and its testsuite are GPL-3.0; this repo is BSL 1.1.
# Their test TEXT is NEVER committed here. It is fetched on demand by scripts/fetch-gnucobol-tests.ps1 into
# this ignored tree. What we DO commit is ours alone: the retrieval script, the .at extractor, the adapter
# test project, and tests/external/gnucobol-expectations.json (independently-authored FACTS about cases —
# per-case classification + our §-cited rationale — never their source or their expected text).
tests/external/gnucobol/
tests/external/*.tar.*
tests/external/*.7z
tests/external/*.zip
# WHERE THE LINE SITS (owner decision 2026-07-19): the substantial expressive content — their COBOL test
# SOURCE and their EXPECTED OUTPUT text — is never committed. Short factual GROUP TITLES and KEYWORDS are
# citable identification (the same nominative use an article describing the suite would make), so the
# differential report and the expectations ledger MAY carry them. Case IDs ("syn_move:38") are coordinates
# we compute. Net effect: our reports are committable; their corpus is not.
# Python bytecode caches, wherever a script imports a module (the evidence scripts import from their own directory)
__pycache__/
# Regenerable output of scripts/gnucobol_differential.py (re-run to recreate). NOT a licensing
# exclusion — per the owner's 2026-07-19 ruling its case titles/keywords are citable; it is simply
# generated, and it is BULKY (it carries every case's title, keywords and our full first diagnostic).
# ⛔ THE COMMITTED ARTIFACT IS tests/external/gnucobol-verdict-baseline.tsv — one row per case,
# id/tier/verdict, all three columns OURS (owner decision 2026-08-04: "names+verdicts is our generated
# results, okay to commit"). It exists so a per-case flip is a ONE-LINE git diff; the four summary totals
# cannot detect offsetting flips and for a long time "0 per-case flips" was asserted from totals alone.
# `battery.sh` gates on it and an ABSENT baseline is a RED, not a pass.
tests/external/gnucobol-differential-report.json

# Session convenience files — untracked by convention (feedback_plans_in_repo)
/scratchpad/

# ── Obsidian vault (notes under kb/) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The NOTES under kb/ ARE tracked — a derived, cross-linked knowledge base (see docs/DOC_INDEX.md
# "Derived knowledge base"). Only Obsidian's per-user / volatile state is ignored so pane moves, caches, and
# vendored plugin code don't churn the repo. community-plugins.json (the plugin LIST) stays tracked for reinstall.
# (VAULT/ retired 2026-07-23 — notes relocated to kb/; only the repo-root .obsidian/ rules below apply)

# Obsidian config at the REPO ROOT (vault root became the repo on 2026-07-23 — one vault over the whole project).
# ⛔ NEVER commit the Local REST API key/cert (data.json) or volatile state. community-plugins.json (the plugin LIST,
# at .obsidian/ top level) MAY be committed for reinstall. The generated code-reference notes are a build output.
.obsidian/*
!.obsidian/app.json
!.obsidian/community-plugins.json
# Vault CSS snippets ARE tracked (they shape how generated notes render — e.g. widening the
# grammar-diagram notes). The key/cert (data.json) under plugins/ stays ignored by .obsidian/* above.
!.obsidian/snippets/
.trash/

# Generated code-reference notes (a build output — regenerated from src/ by the vault generator).
kb/Reference/
# Generated grammar railroad diagrams (regenerated from *.g4 by scripts/gen-grammar-diagrams.ps1).
kb/Grammar/
# RENDERED VIEWS (kb/Work PB3026; scripts/rendered_views.py is the ONE registry; DESIGN-test-build-ci.md section 3.17.4):
# the tree holds SOURCES, derived indexes are rendered on demand and never committed, because two queued pull requests
# that each regenerate one collide, and a copy nobody regenerates goes stale. `RenderedViewsDriftTests` and CI's
# `audits` job fail when a registered output is tracked or missing from this list.
# The conformance burn-down over the traceability inventory (scripts/spec/gen_conformance_notes.py). The inventory
# JSON is the SSOT and IS tracked; these notes are its Dataview-queryable projection.
kb/Conformance/
# The drift-rule index (scripts/spec/drift_rules.py --out): query the rules with `drift_rules.py <path>` instead.
docs/DRIFT_RULES.md
# The diagnostics table (scripts/gen-diagnostics-doc.ps1), rendered from DiagnosticCatalog.cs.
docs/DIAGNOSTICS.md
# Generated status page for the owner's "WiseOwl COBOL Conformance Ledger" artifact (scripts/spec/gen_ledger.py).
# A build output for the same reason kb/Conformance/ is: every input it reads IS tracked, so the page can be
# re-derived at will — and committing it would make `--check` red after every landing that moves a row, which
# is a gate people learn to ignore. `ledger-trend.json` IS tracked: the trend series cannot be recomputed from the
# current tree (the hand-written in-flight narrative is gone, kb/Work PB2912). The page is now rendered into the
# coordination directory (<coord>/ledger.html, kb/Work PB2481); this entry stays so a copy the earlier default left in a
# checkout never makes it dirty (a dirty main checkout sends the orchestrator loop to `resume`).
docs/rearchitecture/evidence/conformance-ledger.html

# Machine-local scratch for optional tooling (e.g. an exported TLS cert). Never a build input.
.claude/local/

# NIST CCVS print files (XXXXX0nn placeholders) a CLI probe run from the repo root would drop here (2026-08-18)
/xxxxx0[0-9][0-9].txt
/XXXXX0[0-9][0-9].txt

# BenchmarkDotNet output (tests/Cobol.Net.Benchmarks). The harness writes its Markdown/HTML/CSV reports and
# the per-benchmark projects it generates and builds under this folder; it is a build output, and the numbers
# worth keeping live in tests/Cobol.Net.Benchmarks/README.md instead.
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# Lander/implementer checkpoint files — a worktree artifact, never part of a landing (DEVLOG 1441).
STATUS.md

# The DEVLOG's descending narrative, rendered on demand from DEVLOG/ (`python scripts/devlog.py render --out
# DEVLOG.rendered.md`); the entry files are the source (kb/Work PB3025).
DEVLOG.rendered.md

# The harness's scheduled-tasks lock — a per-session artifact, committed by accident in 8abe9726 and untracked in train 23's record.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# The conformance suites are BUILD OUTPUT (DESIGN-conformance-suite.md §4; kb/Work PB3174): generate.py writes
# suites/<edition>/manifest.json, suites/wiseowl/manifest.json and suites/completeness.json from the tests' headers.
conformance-suite/suites/
# A harness run's results are OUTPUT too (DESIGN-conformance-suite.md §5; kb/Work PB3175): run.py writes
# results/<compiler>/results.json and junit.xml; a compiler's recorded verdicts are baselines/, which is tracked.
conformance-suite/results/
